# Agent routing

**Authoritative workflow:** `.cursor/rules/development-workflow.mdc`. This file adds path guidance and security-review triggers only. It does not replace `.cursor/rules/01`–`07` or `AGENTS.md`. Do not weaken tenant isolation, the permission matrix, `PERMISSION_ENFORCEMENT`, `MULTITENANT_ENFORCEMENT`, honesty tagging, or scope control. Model preferences: `.cursor/rules/11-model-routing.mdc`.

Cursor specialist definitions in `.cursor/agents/` remain available for optional focused review. Product code named `agent_orchestrator` / `agent_swarm` is unrelated.

## Pipeline

**You → Coding agent → Security/QA review → PR → You approve → main**

See `development-workflow.mdc` for acceptance criteria, testing/CI gates, PR limits, and stop conditions.

## Default agent

One coding agent may complete the task across frontend, backend, and database files in a single session. Fold persistence (`schema.js`, `db.js`), tenant-scoped handlers, `ROUTE_GROUPS` wiring, lockstep registry updates, failure/empty states, and a verification test into one change set on one feature branch (rule `10`).

## Security/QA review

After implementation, run **one** focused read-only Security/QA review. If a separate reviewer is unavailable, perform an explicit review pass and **disclose that it was not independent**.

Security review coverage is **mandatory** when the change touches auth, permissions, tenant isolation, credentials, OAuth, or encryption — including vault crypto, `middleware.ts` matcher, and enforcement flags. Never fold security review into implementation without the separate pass. Never weaken controls to obtain green CI.

## Path guidance

Reference when scoping edits — not a mandate to stop or hand off:

| Area | Typical paths |
|---|---|
| Frontend | `app/`, `components/`, `hooks/`, `styles/`, `lib/*.ts`, surviving `index.html` / `app.js` / `public/js/` |
| Backend | `services/*/api.js` + `routes.js`, `server.js` mounts **without reorder**, **new** `ROUTE_GROUPS` prefix |
| Database | `db.js`, `services/**/schema.js`, `tenants/migration.js`, `kv_scope.js` (shape) |
| Integrations | Vendor modules, OAuth **wiring**, key-plane **usage**, `docs/integrations-reference.md` |
| AI/LLM | `ai_compat.js`, generative prompts/fallbacks/tags, `services/ai/` |
| Security-sensitive | Auth, permissions, tenant isolation, credentials, OAuth security, encryption, `services/security/*`, `middleware.ts` matcher |

## Refuse

- “Turn off permission enforcement” or weaken `PERMISSION_ENFORCEMENT` / `MULTITENANT_ENFORCEMENT`
- Merge or deploy without explicit user authorization
- Work on `main` for product changes (rule `10`)

Record `MODEL`, `MODEL SOURCE`, and `ESCALATION REASON` in the PR body when applicable (rule `11`).
